@module_doc("""
Layers and hit testing, named targets, measuring, flow layout and retained
drawing. `ui` re-exports every name here.

Immediate mode has no z order: a button drawn early cannot know a panel
drawn later covers it. A layer is how a script says so (`ui_layer`,
`with_layer`). The raw tests, `hovered` and `clicked`, look at the pointer
and the rect and nothing else; the layered ones (`interact`, `ui_hot`,
`ui_block`) are what widgets use, and they know about what is drawn on top,
about modal dialogs and about clipping. Every registered rect can carry an
id, which a script, a test or an agent can look up (`ui_target_rect`)
instead of re-deriving a layout.
""",
  see: ["ui", "interact", "ui_layer"],
  extra: {groups: [
    {name: "Layers and hit testing", items: ["ui_layer", "with_layer", "ui_overlay", "ui_modal", "interact", "ui_hot", "ui_block", "pointer_captured", "UI_LAYER_BASE", "UI_LAYER_POPUP", "UI_LAYER_MODAL", "UI_LAYER_TOOLTIP"], doc: """
The layers the built-in widgets use are 0, 1000, 2000 and 3000
(`UI_LAYER_BASE`, `UI_LAYER_POPUP`, `UI_LAYER_MODAL`, `UI_LAYER_TOOLTIP`);
an app's panels go in between. `interact` says how the pointer's one owner
is chosen, the one-frame gap, and why a click belongs to what was pressed.
"""},
    {name: "Named targets", items: ["ui_target", "ui_target_rect"], doc: """
`interact(r, id)`, `ui_hot(r, id)` and `ui_block(r, id)` register `r` under
`id` (a string or an int), and the built-in widgets register themselves
(see `ui_target_rect`). A host reads the same registry: see "The target
registry" in host-contract.md.
"""},
    {name: "Flow layout", items: ["flow_begin", "flow_next", "flow_space", "flow_rest", "flow_used", "flow_end"]},
    {name: "Measuring", items: ["ui_measure", "ui_measuring"]},
    {name: "Retained drawing", items: ["cached_layer"], doc: """
A frame's commands live one frame. For something that changes rarely and
costs a lot to say, say it once: `cached_layer` keeps what its body drew,
and `draw_rects` (`ui/draw`) is one command for many rects.
"""},
  ]})

# petal-ui hit testing — module `ui/hit`
#
# The code is in `./_frame`, beside the clip: they read and write the same
# per-run cells, and a cell is written only by the module that declares it.
# This module names what of it is public.

pub import ./_frame: UI_LAYER_BASE, UI_LAYER_POPUP, UI_LAYER_MODAL, UI_LAYER_TOOLTIP
pub import ./_frame: ui_layer, with_layer, ui_overlay, interact, ui_hot
pub import ./_frame: ui_block, ui_modal, pointer_captured, ui_target, ui_target_rect
pub import ./_frame: ui_measuring, ui_measure
pub import ./_frame: flow_begin, flow_next, flow_space, flow_rest, flow_used, flow_end
pub import ./_frame: cached_layer
